SUMMARY:🌿🌊 TORONTO ISLANDS SUMMER WALK (9KM) 🌊🌿
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n# 🌿
 🌊 TORONTO ISLANDS SUMMER WALK (9KM) 🌊🌿\n\n### Island Paths\, Skyl
 ine Views & Toronto's Best Urban Escape\n\nThere is something magical abou
 t the Toronto Islands.\nJust minutes from downtown\, the noise of the city
  disappears and is replaced by tree-lined paths\, open green spaces\, quie
 t cottages\, and some of the best skyline views anywhere in Toronto. It fe
 els like you've escaped the city without ever leaving it.\n\nJoin us for a
  relaxed summer walk across the Toronto Islands as we explore **Hanlan's P
 oint\, Centre Island\, and Ward's Island**\, enjoying beautiful scenery\, 
 fresh air\, and great conversation along the way.\n\nThe Toronto Islands h
 ave a fascinating history. Originally connected to the mainland as a long 
 sandbar peninsula\, a powerful storm in 1858 permanently separated the lan
 d from Toronto\, creating the islands we know today.\nOver the years they'
 ve been home to amusement parks\, summer cottages\, and the unique island 
 community that still exists today on Ward's Island.\n\nThis is **not** a f
 ormal historical tour.\n\nIt's a social walk with beautiful scenery\, fres
 h air\, and great conversation.\n\n📲 **Don't Forget to join our WhatsAp
 p Group – [CLICK HERE!](📲 Join Our WhatsApp Group: Click here to join
 )**\n\n***\n\n## 🚶‍♂️ What We'll Do\n\nWe'll take the **11:15 AM 
 Hanlan's Point Ferry** to the islands and begin our walk.\n\nOur route wil
 l take us through:\n\n🌿 Hanlan's Point\n🌳 Centre Island\n🏡 Ward's
  Island\n📸 Several incredible skyline viewpoints\n🌊 Beautiful waterf
 ront pathways\n\nWe'll stop throughout the walk to enjoy the scenery for a
  30mins break\, take photos\, and experience one of Toronto's most unique 
 parks.\nFeel free to bring a snack or something small to share during one 
 of our breaks.\n\n**Please Note:** Although we'll pass several beaches\, w
 e won't be stopping at them during this event. We have a route to follow a
 nd a ferry to catch! Instead\, we'll enjoy our break at one of the islands
 ' spectacular skyline lookout points\, where you can relax\, have a snack\
 , and take some amazing photos. If you'd rather spend time at the beach\, 
 you're welcome to do so after the walk\, but the group won't be waiting as
  we continue on our planned route.\n\nOur return ferry will be the **2:45 
 PM Ward's Island Ferry** back to downtown Toronto.\n\nExpect approximately
  **3½ to 4 hours** including the ferry rides and breaks.\n\n***\n\n## ☀
 ️ Weather & Expectations\n\nThis event happens in typical summer weather
 .\nThe islands are often cooler and breezier than downtown Toronto\, so br
 inging a light sweater is never a bad idea.\nThe only reason we would canc
 el is because of severe weather or thunderstorms.\n\nThis is a social walk
 —not a guided historical tour. I'll share interesting facts along the wa
 y\, but the focus is enjoying the islands together.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meet
 up Details\n\n**📍 Meetup Location:**\n**INSIDE the Jack Layton Ferry Te
 rminal after your ticket has been scanned.**\n\nWe are meeting **inside** 
 the paid waiting area **beside the washrooms**.\n**Please do NOT wait outs
 ide the terminal.**\n\nOnce your ferry ticket has been scanned\, walk into
  the waiting area and you'll find me beside the washrooms wearing my **Moo
 se Hat**.\n\n⏰ **Meetup Time:** **11:00 AM**\n🚢 **Hanlan's Point Ferr
 y LEAVES AT:** **11:15 AM**\n\nOnce we board the ferry\, it is extremely d
 ifficult for late arrivals to catch up with the group.\n🚢 **Return Ferr
 y:** **2:45 PM from Ward's Island**\n🎟️ **Ferry Ticket:** *$9.40*\n\n
 You must purchase your ferry ticket before signing up.\n[CLICK HERE FOR TI
 CKETS!](https://secure.toronto.ca/FerryTicketOnline/tickets2/index.jsp)\n\
 n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$5 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧
  **[mathewmaclean@hotmail.com](mailto:mathewmaclean@hotmail.com)**\n\nThis
  fee helps support the group and allows us to continue organizing events l
 ike this. Thank you for supporting community! 💖\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What 
 to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🥨 A snack\n🧥
  A light sweater\n🕶️ Sunglasses\n📸 Camera or phone for photos\n\n*
 **\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis group is open to anyone who wants t
 o be social and make friends—whether single or not.\n\nWe also host:\n
 🎬 Movies\n🚶 Walks & hikes\n🎭 Arts & culture outings\n🍽️ Rest
 aurant gatherings\nThere's always something happening.\n\n***\n\n**REMEMBE
 R:** You're welcome to just show up on the day if you're unsure about your
  schedule.\nSometimes plans change and events may need to be cancelled\, s
 o please keep an eye on updates.\n\n***\n\n👤 **Organizer:** Mathew\nQue
 stions? Post on the event wall or email\n📧 **[torontomoviesandoutings@h
 otmail.com](mailto:torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com)**\n\n**Come for th
 e island paths.**\n**Stay for the skyline.**\n\n**Leave feeling like you s
 pent the day on vacation—without ever leaving Toronto.** 🌿🌊\n\n***
