SUMMARY:🌿🌳 SUMMER EVENING WALK: GUS HARRIS TRAIL 🌳🌿
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n# 🌿
 🌳 SUMMER EVENING WALK: GUS HARRIS TRAIL 🌳🌿\n\n**A Hidden Ravine\,
  Easy Walking & Great Conversation**\nSometimes the best parts of Toronto 
 are the ones most people drive right past.\n\nJoin us for a relaxed summer
  evening walk along the Gus Harris Trail\, one of Toronto's hidden ravine 
 trails that follows the peaceful Taylor-Massey Creek through Scarborough a
 nd East York.\n\nThis isn't a challenging hike—it's an easy\, mostly fla
 t walk that's perfect for anyone looking to enjoy nature\, get some fresh 
 air\, and spend an evening with great people.\n\nThe real purpose of the w
 alk isn't simply reaching the end of the trail.\nIt's creating the space t
 o slow down\, have conversations\, meet new people\, and enjoy a few hours
  away from the busyness of everyday life.\n\nAlong the way we'll follow th
 e creek\, enjoy the shade of the ravine\, and discover one of Toronto's qu
 ieter green spaces that many people never even realize exists.\n\n✨ **Fu
 n Fact:** Taylor-Massey Creek is named after two prominent Toronto familie
 s. The Taylor family owned the famous Don Valley Brick Works\, now known a
 s Evergreen Brick Works—one of Toronto's most successful environmental r
 evitalization projects.\n\n📲 **Join Our WhatsApp Group:**[ Click here t
 o join](https://chat.whatsapp.com/DRFTkxRlHS4B3IL1lMleUd)\n\n***\n\n## 
 🚶‍♂️ What We'll Do\n\nWe'll spend about two hours enjoying an eas
 y walk along the trail\, taking our time\, chatting\, and getting to know 
 one another.\n\nThis is a social walk—not a race.\n\nThere are very few 
 hills\, making it a comfortable walk for most people with a reasonable lev
 el of fitness.\nWe'll finish back where we started before the park closes 
 for the evening.\n\n***\n\n## ☀️ Weather & Expectations\n\nThis walk w
 ill happen rain or shine unless severe weather makes it unsafe.\nPlease we
 ar comfortable walking shoes and dress appropriately for the weather.\n\nT
 he focus isn't covering as much ground as possible.\nThe focus is spending
  a relaxing evening outdoors with good company.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup D
 etails\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** Outside Victoria Park Subway Station b
 y Victoria Park road.\n🫎 I'll be wearing my Moose Hat.\n⏰ **Meetup Ti
 me:** **6:00 PM**\nI will only wait **5 minutes.**\nEarly is on time.\nOn 
 time is late.\n\n🏁 **End Spot:** Victoria Park Subway Station (before t
 he cemetery gates close).\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$5 cash in 
 person or e-transfer**\n📧 **[mathewmaclean@hotmail.com](mailto:mathewma
 clean@hotmail.com)**\nThis fee helps support the group and allows us to co
 ntinue organizing events like this. Thank you for supporting community! 
 💖\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walki
 ng shoes\n🥨 A snack (optional)\n🌞 Bug spray or sunscreen if needed\n
 \n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis group is open to anyone who want
 s to be social and make friends—whether single or not.\n\nWe also host:\
 n🎬 Movies\n🚶 Walks & hikes\n🎭 Arts & culture outings\n🍽️ Res
 taurant gatherings\nThere's always something happening.\n\n***\n\n**REMEMB
 ER:** You're welcome to just show up on the day if you're unsure about you
 r schedule.\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be cancelled
 —please keep an eye on updates.\n\n***\n\n👤 **Organizer:** Mathew\nQu
 estions? Post on the event wall or email:\n📧 **[torontomoviesandoutings
 @hotmail.com](mailto:torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com)**\n\n**Come for 
 the trail.**\n**Stay for the conversation.**\n**Leave having discovered th
 at sometimes**\n\n**Toronto's best hidden places aren't the destination—
 they're simply where new friendships begin.**
